{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ShortestPathTree","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree.swift#L26","fileName":"ShortestPathTree.swift"},"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shortest paths from one or more sources: for each reached vertex, its distance, its parent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the edge from the parent (a forest when there are several sources, LEMON’s “shortest path tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(forest)”)."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(toIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/path(to:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The first relaxation to a vertex’s final distance wins. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"parent(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest-path predecessor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" along","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order among equals.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Several sources.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each source starts at distance zero with no parent. Dijkstra’s algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no parent even when another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one super-source (NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_bellman_ford"},{"type":"text","text":"): a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/distance(to:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The length of a shortest path from a source to ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when no path reaches it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or every path is longer than the cutoff).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"distance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"distance(to:)","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree\/distance(to:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)"},"doc://ShortestPaths/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/parent(ofIndex:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The index of the parent of the vertex with index ","type":"text"},{"code":"index","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"parent(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"parent"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"ofIndex"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":") -